// Hadamard matrices of the orders 4*m, m odd, used by the randomized Hadamard transform
// (ggml-hadamard.c, ggml-cuda/rht.cuh), plus order 40.
//
// Each matrix is its source's +/- rows, verbatim, one literal per row, unnormalized and row-major.
// The includer defines GGML_HAD_DECL(K) as the declarator of the K*K+1 char array and expands
// GGML_HAD_ORDERS(X) for the index; the CUDA code includes this file once per storage class.
//
// All orders except 12 are from N. J. A. Sloane's library of Hadamard matrices,
// http://neilsloane.com/hadamard/ (20, 28 and 40 are also in Tri Dao's code_gen.py).
// Order 12 is from Tri Dao's fast-hadamard-transform, csrc/code_gen.py,
